version: 0.1.0
abstract: Shen nang yi jue (1874), published by Ji ao xuan at [Amoy] according to
  the Bodleian catalogue, is Patrick Manson’s Chinese translation and adaptation of
  a work by Thomas Blizard Curling. Its English preface, signed at Amoy, describes
  additional anatomical material and observations by Manson. The book discusses historical
  conditions of the testis, scrotum and spermatic cord, case records, surgery and
  illustrated explanations, with Chinese and English prefaces, a contents list and
  a bilingual vocabulary. It can support research on late Qing medical translation,
  terminology and medical illustration. This version provides JSON, TXT and TEI for
  497 original printed text, caption and labelled illustration faces from the three
  bound volumes of Bodleian Sinica 1845, retaining their physical order and conflicting
  printed volume numbers. It is an AI-assisted initial transcription with uncertain
  and unresolved readings; comparison with independent readings and full human collation
  have not been completed for this version.
